  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.Utils.
    MemberName: PutNullableUnmanaged<T>
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - value
    ParamDocs:
    - The nullable value to write into the buffer. If , only a  flag is written.
    Summary: "Writes a nullable value of type `T` into the internal byte buffer at
      the current position,\n first writing a bool indicating whether the value is
      present,\n and then writing the value itself if it exists.  Advances the position
      by 1 byte for the presence flag plus\n the size of `T` if the value is present."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames:
    - T
